{"id": "EUVD-2026-93155", "enisaUuid": "3209bce8-85b1-3dea-a2c7-10923cd59693", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmemstick: ms_block: destroy io_queue workqueue on removal\n\nmsb_init_disk() creates the per-card ordered workqueue msb->io_queue with\nalloc_ordered_workqueue(). It is torn down with destroy_workqueue() only\non the init error path; msb_remove() never destroys it. msb_stop() merely\nflushes the queue, and neither msb_data_clear() nor put_disk() free it. As\na result every card insert/remove cycle leaks the workqueue and its\nkworker, exhausting kernel memory over repeated cycles.\n\nDestroy the workqueue in msb_remove() after the disk has been removed and\nthe queue drained.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ff795163f37109a134b5a421558530f8d091544", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/19c3da6621a253f1f8b937ed91bc22330a930d9c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a2e7cdc0880e735aff0968ee402f2c92a992b9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6611f78ec3fd4b33a00bfda20725b254a22979f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f222bb8c30cf5699c560b29179ff2bddcac1f950", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/90af7fde083e1b22c349c3a8b1626728e44e474c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4xvx-jjq9-8pfx", "CVE-2026-98227"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1413627f-be08-3759-94fb-75ffd9a69e2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "20641afe-e56a-3401-804a-1d50e8ff6875", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "39be48bb-9237-36fb-810c-2fe3f4b07b05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ab30494bc4f3bc1ea4659b7c5d97c5218554a63 <19c3da6621a253f1f8b937ed91bc22330a930d9c"}, {"id": "4fbec3e2-4ce7-3065-b1a8-dae8f888440d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.12"}, {"id": "6c882859-ec16-309d-aa33-04cf0b52a0de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "739a1fd1-6717-3755-90a4-5d370fc28214", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "92d31084-777b-391a-a3f8-fc923b2a4f23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ab30494bc4f3bc1ea4659b7c5d97c5218554a63 <0ff795163f37109a134b5a421558530f8d091544"}, {"id": "9eadf02a-dac8-3c6e-912f-c981cb8af0e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "bdc071a4-335f-3452-b4a2-b0306902b927", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "c32a62a3-00c3-3a68-9761-ed75d093353f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ab30494bc4f3bc1ea4659b7c5d97c5218554a63 <9a2e7cdc0880e735aff0968ee402f2c92a992b9b"}, {"id": "ce6465d3-27e6-38e8-a941-ee2a7a123960", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d0dfd430-18ba-39d0-8b72-0d4e78f9c177", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ab30494bc4f3bc1ea4659b7c5d97c5218554a63 <6611f78ec3fd4b33a00bfda20725b254a22979f6"}, {"id": "f0ce9b56-4463-3d07-874b-a4742e220b76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ab30494bc4f3bc1ea4659b7c5d97c5218554a63 <90af7fde083e1b22c349c3a8b1626728e44e474c"}, {"id": "f7cbe93c-a51a-3254-be44-6a10b7ad8b6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ab30494bc4f3bc1ea4659b7c5d97c5218554a63 <f222bb8c30cf5699c560b29179ff2bddcac1f950"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1ffaae7e-3568-34d8-9889-49dd4f34e73f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}